#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:4
msgid "点群と空間群"
msgstr "Point Groups and Space Groups"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:6
msgid ""
":ref:`結晶の対称操作<crystal-symmetry-operations>`\\ を使い、空間群と点群が何を分類するかを "
"整理する。格子と原子配置の両方を考えることで、同じ\\ :ref:`ブラベー格子型<bravais-lattice-types>`\\ "
"の結晶で対称性の違いが 生じる理由も見えてくる。"
msgstr ""
"We use :ref:`crystal symmetry operations <crystal-symmetry-operations>`\\"
"  to explain what space groups and point groups classify. Considering "
"both the lattice and the atomic arrangement also reveals why crystals of "
"the same \\ :ref:`Bravais lattice type <bravais-lattice-types>`\\  can "
"have different symmetries."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:10
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`結晶の対称操作<crystal-symmetry-operations>`、:ref:`ブラベー格子型"
"<bravais-lattice-types>`、 :ref:`分率座標<coordinates>`、:ref:`方向指数とMiller指数"
"<crystal-directions-planes>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Crystal symmetry operations <crystal-symmetry-"
"operations>`, :ref:`Bravais lattice types <bravais-lattice-types>`, "
":ref:`fractional coordinates <coordinates>`, and :ref:`direction indices "
"and Miller indices <crystal-directions-planes>`."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:13
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:15
msgid "空間群・並進部分群・点群の関係を説明し、らせん操作と映進操作が点群に何を残すかを示す。"
msgstr ""
"Explain the relationship between a space group, its translation subgroup,"
" and its point group, and identify what remains of screw operations and "
"glide operations in the point group."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:16
msgid "点群の操作から、等価な方向と面の族を求める。"
msgstr ""
"Use point group operations to find families of equivalent directions and "
"planes."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:17
msgid "非対称単位の原子と対称操作から、単位胞内の原子座標を展開する。"
msgstr ""
"Generate the atomic coordinates in a unit cell from the atoms in the "
"asymmetric unit and the symmetry operations."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:18
msgid "反転対称性から、自発分極が許されるかを判定する。"
msgstr ""
"Use inversion symmetry to determine whether spontaneous polarization is "
"allowed."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:23
msgid "空間群と並進部分群"
msgstr "Space Groups and Translation Subgroups"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:25
msgid ""
"ある結晶の原子配置を保つ操作をすべて集めたものが **空間群** :math:`\\mathcal G` である。 このうち線形部分が "
":math:`I` の操作、つまり結晶を保つ純粋な並進の集まりを並進部分群 :math:`\\mathcal T` "
"と呼ぶ。対応する並進ベクトルの集合が、その結晶の格子である。 例えばF中心の慣用単位胞を用いる場合は、胞の辺を整数倍した並進に加え、 "
":ref:`中心並進<centring-translation>`\\ も :math:`\\mathcal T` に含まれる。 "
"三次元の結晶の空間群は230種類に分類される。"
msgstr ""
"The **space group** :math:`\\mathcal G` consists of all operations that "
"preserve the atomic arrangement of a crystal. The operations with linear "
"part :math:`I`, namely the pure translations that preserve the crystal, "
"form the translation subgroup :math:`\\mathcal T`. The corresponding "
"translation vectors form the lattice of the crystal. For example, if an "
"F-centered conventional cell is used, the :ref:`centering translations "
"<centring-translation>`\\  are included in :math:`\\mathcal T` together "
"with translations by integer multiples of the cell edges. The space "
"groups of three-dimensional crystals are classified into 230 types."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:34
msgid ""
"空間群の操作には、回転に軸方向の並進が伴うらせん操作や、鏡映に面に沿った並進が 伴う映進操作もある。例えば :math:`z` "
"軸のまわりの180度回転と :math:`c/2` の軸方向 並進を一緒に行う :math:`2_1` らせん操作は、2回繰り返すと "
":math:`c` の純粋な並進になる。 原子の座標を展開したり回折の反射条件を調べたりするときは、この並進部分も必要になる。"
msgstr ""
"Space group operations also include screw operations, which combine "
"rotation with translation along the axis, and glide operations, which "
"combine reflection with translation along the plane. For example, "
"combining a 180° rotation about the :math:`z` axis with an axial "
"translation of :math:`c/2` gives a :math:`2_1` screw operation. Applying "
"it twice gives a pure translation of :math:`c`. The translational part is"
" needed when generating atomic coordinates or checking reflection "
"conditions in diffraction."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:42
msgid "点群と空間群の関係"
msgstr "Relation Between Point Groups and Space Groups"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:44
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"空間群の各操作 :math:`\\{Q\\mid\\boldsymbol t\\}` から線形部分 :math:`Q` を取り出すと **点群**"
" :math:`\\mathcal P` が得られる。式 :eq:`crystal-symmetry-composition` に よれば、同じ "
":math:`Q` を持つ二つの操作の差は純粋な格子並進である。点群の一つの "
"操作には、格子並進の違いだけをもつ空間群の操作の組が対応する。この関係を :math:`\\mathcal G/\\mathcal "
"T\\simeq\\mathcal P` と書く。 三次元の結晶学的な点群は32種類である。"
msgstr ""
"Taking each space group operation :math:`\\{Q\\mid\\boldsymbol t\\}` and "
"extracting its linear part :math:`Q` gives the **point group** "
":math:`\\mathcal P`. According to Equation :eq:`crystal-symmetry-"
"composition`, two operations with the same :math:`Q` differ by a pure "
"lattice translation. A single point group operation corresponds to a set "
"of space group operations that differ only by lattice translations. We "
"write this relationship as :math:`\\mathcal G/\\mathcal T\\simeq\\mathcal"
" P`. There are 32 crystallographic point groups in three dimensions."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:51
msgid ""
"先の :math:`2_1` らせん操作の例では、点群に残るのは180度回転である。同じ点群の "
"操作でも、空間群では純粋な回転として現れる場合と、らせん操作として現れる場合がある。 :ref:`対称操作による波数の変換<kpoint-"
"symmetry-mapping>`\\ には線形部分を使い、 :ref:`構造因子<scattering-structure-"
"factor>`\\ には原子の位置に応じた散乱波の位相が入る。"
msgstr ""
"In the preceding example of the :math:`2_1` screw operation, the point "
"group retains the 180° rotation. The same point group operation can occur"
" in a space group as a pure rotation or as a screw operation. The linear "
"part is used in the :ref:`transformation of wave vectors under symmetry "
"operations <kpoint-symmetry-mapping>`\\ , whereas the :ref:`structure "
"factor <scattering-structure-factor>`\\  includes the phases of the "
"scattered waves, which depend on the atomic positions."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:61
msgid "|equivalent-direction-families|"
msgstr "Families of Equivalent Directions and Planes"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:63
msgid ""
":ref:`方向指数<crystal-direction-index>` :math:`[uvw]` は1本の方向、\\ "
":ref:`Miller指数<lattice-planes-miller>` :math:`(hkl)` "
"は1組の平行な格子面を指す。結晶の対称操作で互いに移り合う2つの方向に沿って見ると、原子の並びは同じである。外場や磁気秩序を含めて、測定するときの結晶の状態もその対称操作を保つなら、その方向に沿って測る物性も等しい。例えば立方晶では、:math:`z`"
" 軸まわりの90度回転が :math:`[100]` を :math:`[010]` "
"へ移す。このような方向や面の集まりを族と呼び、ひとまとめにした記号で書く（:numref:`lt-index-"
"brackets`。International Tables for Crystallography, Vol. A (2006), "
"`§1.1.4 <https://it.iucr.org/Ab/ch1o1v0001/sec1o1o4.pdf>`__）。"
msgstr ""
"The :ref:`direction indices <crystal-direction-index>` :math:`[uvw]` "
"specify a single direction, and the \\ :ref:`Miller indices <lattice-"
"planes-miller>` :math:`(hkl)` specify a set of parallel lattice planes. "
"Viewed along two directions related by a crystal symmetry operation, the "
"atoms have the same arrangement. The physical properties measured along "
"those directions are also equal if the state of the crystal during "
"measurement still preserves that operation, taking any external field or "
"magnetic order into account. For example, in a cubic crystal, a 90° "
"rotation about the :math:`z` axis maps :math:`[100]` to :math:`[010]`. A "
"set of such directions or planes is called a family and is denoted by one"
" symbol (see :numref:`lt-index-brackets` and International Tables for "
"Crystallography, Vol. A (2006), `§1.1.4 "
"<https://it.iucr.org/Ab/ch1o1v0001/sec1o1o4.pdf>`__)."

