msgstr "The set of planes related to :math:`(hkl)` by symmetry operations"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:81
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"どの方向が等価かは、結晶の点群で決まる。対称操作 :math:`\\{Q\\mid\\boldsymbol t\\}` "
"の線形部分を格子基底で表した行列を :math:`W=A^{-1}QA`\\ （:eq:`crystal-symmetry-"
"fractional`）とする。方向と面法線は2点の差で決まるベクトルなので、並進 :math:`\\boldsymbol t` "
"は作用しない。方向は :math:`QA\\boldsymbol u=A(W\\boldsymbol u)` に移る。:math:`Q` "
"は直交行列なので :math:`Q=Q^{-\\mathsf T}=A^{-\\mathsf T}W^{-\\mathsf "
"T}A^{\\mathsf T}` と書ける。これを使うと、面法線は :math:`QB\\boldsymbol h=2\\pi "
"A^{-\\mathsf T}W^{-\\mathsf T}\\boldsymbol h=B(W^{-\\mathsf "
"T}\\boldsymbol h)` に移る。点群 :math:`\\mathcal P` の各操作から作る :math:`W` の集合を "
":math:`\\mathcal W` と書けば、"
msgstr ""
"The crystal's point group determines which directions are equivalent. For"
" the symmetry operation :math:`\\{Q\\mid\\boldsymbol t\\}`, let "
":math:`W=A^{-1}QA`\\  be the matrix of its linear part in the lattice "
"basis (Equation :eq:`crystal-symmetry-fractional`). Directions and plane "
"normals are determined by differences between two points, so the "
"translation :math:`\\boldsymbol t` has no effect on them. The direction "
"maps to :math:`QA\\boldsymbol u=A(W\\boldsymbol u)`. Since :math:`Q` is "
"orthogonal, we can write :math:`Q=Q^{-\\mathsf T}=A^{-\\mathsf "
"T}W^{-\\mathsf T}A^{\\mathsf T}`. It follows that the plane normal maps "
"to :math:`QB\\boldsymbol h=2\\pi A^{-\\mathsf T}W^{-\\mathsf "
"T}\\boldsymbol h=B(W^{-\\mathsf T}\\boldsymbol h)`. For each operation in"
" the point group :math:`\\mathcal P`, form the corresponding matrix "
":math:`W` and denote the set of these matrices by :math:`\\mathcal W`. "
"Then"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:83
msgid ""
"\\langle uvw\\rangle=\\{\\,W\\boldsymbol u\\mid W\\in\\mathcal "
"W\\,\\},\\qquad\n"
"\\{hkl\\}=\\{\\,W^{-\\mathsf T}\\boldsymbol h\\mid W\\in\\mathcal W\\,\\}."
msgstr ""
"\\langle uvw\\rangle=\\{\\,W\\boldsymbol u\\mid W\\in\\mathcal "
"W\\,\\},\\qquad\n"
"\\{hkl\\}=\\{\\,W^{-\\mathsf T}\\boldsymbol h\\mid W\\in\\mathcal W\\,\\}."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:89
msgid "並進が作用しないので、らせん軸や映進面は、対応する回転や鏡映と同じ族を作る。"
msgstr ""
"Since translations have no effect on the vectors, screw axes and glide "
"planes yield the same families as the corresponding rotations and "
"reflections."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:91
msgid ""
"族に含まれる方向の数は点群によって変わる。立方晶の点群 :math:`m\\bar3m`\\ "
"（48個の操作）は、立方慣用単位胞の基底で、成分の並べ替えと符号の反転をすべて含む。このため "
":math:`\\langle100\\rangle` は "
":math:`\\pm[100]`、:math:`\\pm[010]`、:math:`\\pm[001]` "
"の6方向、:math:`\\langle110\\rangle` は12方向、:math:`\\langle111\\rangle` "
"は8方向になる。正方晶の点群 :math:`4/mmm`\\ （16個）には :math:`c` 軸を :math:`a` "
"軸へ移す操作が無い。:math:`\\langle100\\rangle` は :math:`\\pm[100]` と "
":math:`\\pm[010]` の4方向だけで、:math:`\\pm[001]` は別の族 "
":math:`\\langle001\\rangle` になる。極性の点群 :math:`4mm`\\ （8個）には :math:`c` "
"軸を反転する操作も無く、:math:`[001]` と :math:`[00\\bar1]` は等価でない。:math:`[uvw]` と "
":math:`[\\bar u\\bar v\\bar w]` が同じ族に入るのは、反転のように :math:`\\boldsymbol u` を"
" :math:`-\\boldsymbol u` へ移す操作が点群にあるときに限る（\\ :ref:`反転対称性と自発分極<inversion-"
"and-polarization>`\\ ）。"
msgstr ""
"The number of directions in a family depends on the point group. In the "
"basis of the cubic conventional cell, the cubic point group "
":math:`m\\bar3m`\\  (48 operations) includes every permutation of the "
"components and every combination of sign changes. Thus "
":math:`\\langle100\\rangle` contains the six directions "
":math:`\\pm[100]`, :math:`\\pm[010]`, and :math:`\\pm[001]`, "
":math:`\\langle110\\rangle` contains 12 directions, and "
":math:`\\langle111\\rangle` contains eight. The tetragonal point group "
":math:`4/mmm`\\  (16 operations) has no operation that maps the :math:`c`"
" axis to the :math:`a` axis. The family :math:`\\langle100\\rangle` "
"contains only the four directions :math:`\\pm[100]` and "
":math:`\\pm[010]`, and :math:`\\pm[001]` form a separate family "
":math:`\\langle001\\rangle`. The polar point group :math:`4mm`\\  (eight "
"operations) also has no operation that reverses the :math:`c` axis, so "
":math:`[001]` and :math:`[00\\bar1]` are inequivalent. The directions "
":math:`[uvw]` and :math:`[\\bar u\\bar v\\bar w]` belong to the same "
"family only if the point group has an operation such as inversion that "
"maps :math:`\\boldsymbol u` to :math:`-\\boldsymbol u` (see \\ "
":ref:`inversion symmetry and spontaneous polarization <inversion-and-"
"polarization>`\\ )."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"族の要素は、数字の並べ替えと符号の反転とは限らない。立方慣用単位胞の直交基底では :math:`W` が直交行列で "
":math:`W^{-\\mathsf T}=W` なので、:math:`\\langle uvw\\rangle` と "
":math:`\\{uvw\\}` "
"は同じ指数の組を並べる。六方晶の基底（:math:`\\gamma=120^\\circ`）では、:math:`c` 軸まわりの60度回転が "
":math:`\\boldsymbol a_1` を :math:`\\boldsymbol a_1+\\boldsymbol a_2` "
"へ移す。点群 :math:`6/mmm` の :math:`\\langle100\\rangle` は "
":math:`\\pm[100]`、:math:`\\pm[010]`、:math:`\\pm[110]` "
"の6方向、:math:`\\{100\\}` は "
":math:`\\pm(100)`、:math:`\\pm(010)`、:math:`\\pm(1\\bar10)` の6組になる。"
msgstr ""
"The members of a family are not necessarily obtained by permuting the "
"indices and changing their signs. In the orthogonal basis of a cubic "
"conventional cell, :math:`W` is orthogonal and :math:`W^{-\\mathsf T}=W`,"
" so :math:`\\langle uvw\\rangle` and :math:`\\{uvw\\}` list the same "
"index triples. In a hexagonal basis (:math:`\\gamma=120^\\circ`), a 60° "
"rotation about the :math:`c` axis maps :math:`\\boldsymbol a_1` to "
":math:`\\boldsymbol a_1+\\boldsymbol a_2`. For point group :math:`6/mmm`,"
" :math:`\\langle100\\rangle` contains six directions, :math:`\\pm[100]`, "
":math:`\\pm[010]`, and :math:`\\pm[110]`, whereas :math:`\\{100\\}` "
"contains six sets of planes, :math:`\\pm(100)`, :math:`\\pm(010)`, and "
":math:`\\pm(1\\bar10)`."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:98
msgid "非対称単位と原子座標の展開"
msgstr "Asymmetric Unit and Expansion of Atomic Coordinates"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:100
msgid ""
"非対称単位は、空間群の操作で空間全体に展開できる領域である。 :ref:`CIF<lt-cif>` に対称操作と代表原子の\\ "
":ref:`分率座標<coordinates>`\\ がある場合、式 :eq:`crystal-symmetry-fractional` "
"を使って単位胞内の等価な原子を求められる。 単位胞の外に出た座標は、各成分が :math:`[0,1)` "
"に入るよう整数を足し引きして戻す。例えば反転 :math:`(x,y,z)\\mapsto(-x,-y,-z)` を "
":math:`(1/4,1/4,0)` に施すと :math:`(3/4,3/4,0)` と等価な位置が得られる。反転中心の "
":math:`(0,0,0)` にある原子は自分自身に戻るため、1個として数える。"
msgstr ""
"An asymmetric unit is a region from which all of space can be generated "
"by applying the space group operations. If a :ref:`CIF <lt-cif>` contains"
" the symmetry operations and the \\ :ref:`fractional coordinates "
"<coordinates>`\\  of representative atoms, Equation :eq:`crystal-"
"symmetry-fractional` gives the equivalent atoms in the unit cell. Bring "
"coordinates outside the unit cell back into it by adding or subtracting "
"integers so each component lies in :math:`[0,1)`. For example, applying "
"the inversion :math:`(x,y,z)\\mapsto(-x,-y,-z)` to :math:`(1/4,1/4,0)` "
"gives a position equivalent to :math:`(3/4,3/4,0)`. An atom at the "
"inversion center :math:`(0,0,0)` maps onto itself, so count it once."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:108
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-asymmetric-unit-inversion`\\ では、反転で胞外の :math:`(-1/4,-1/4,0)`"
" に移った点を 格子並進 :math:`(1,1,0)` で胞内の :math:`(3/4,3/4,0)` へ戻す。格子並進は結晶全体の配置を "
"保つので、胞内に戻した点も元の原子と対称性で等価である。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`fig-asymmetric-unit-inversion`\\ , inversion sends the point "
"outside the cell to :math:`(-1/4,-1/4,0)`. The lattice translation "
":math:`(1,1,0)` brings it back inside to :math:`(3/4,3/4,0)`. The lattice"
" translation preserves the entire crystal arrangement, so the point "
"brought back into the cell is symmetry-equivalent to the original atom."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:112
msgid "分率座標で(1/4,1/4)の原子を反転し、胞外の(-1/4,-1/4)から(1,1)だけ並進して胞内の(3/4,3/4)を得る。"
msgstr ""
"The atom at fractional coordinates (1/4,1/4) maps by inversion to "
"(-1/4,-1/4) outside the cell. Translation by (1,1) brings it to (3/4,3/4)"
" inside the cell."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:118
msgid ""
":math:`z=0` の断面。白抜きの丸がCIFにあると仮定した代表原子、×が反転直後の位置、 "
"塗りつぶした丸が単位胞内に折り戻した等価な原子である。ひし形は反転中心の原点を示す。"
msgstr ""
"A cross section at :math:`z=0`. The open circle marks the representative "
"atom assumed to be in the CIF, the × marks its position immediately after"
" inversion, and the filled circle marks the equivalent atom brought back "
"into the unit cell. The diamond marks the origin, the inversion center."

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:124
msgid "反転対称性と自発分極"
msgstr "Inversion Symmetry and Spontaneous Polarization"

#: ../../solid/point_and_space_groups.rst:126
msgid ""
"ブラベー格子型は格子点の並びを分類し、空間群はそこに置いた原子配置の対称性を表す。 例えば\\ "
":ref:`チタン酸バリウムの立方晶相<batio3-crystal-phases>`\\ では、反転で 原子配置が保たれる。\\ "
":ref:`自発分極<spontaneous-polarization>`\\ は極性ベクトルなので、反転で符号が変わる。 反転対称な構造では "
":math:`\\boldsymbol P` と :math:`-\\boldsymbol P` が同じ構造の分極を表す。 周期結晶の分極は\\ "
":ref:`分極の量子<fo-polarization-quantum>`\\ の整数倍だけ不定なので、この条件は分極の量子を法として "
":math:`\\boldsymbol P\\equiv-\\boldsymbol P` "
"となり、分極の各成分は0か分極の量子の半分になる。どちらの場合も、 反転対称な構造は\\ :ref:`自発分極をもたない"
"<polarization-inversion>`。自発分極は、反転対称な参照構造からの "
"分極の変化として測られる量だからである。正方晶相では反転対称性が失われ、長軸方向の分極が許される。 "
"実際に分極が生じるか、その大きさがいくらかは、原子変位と電子状態で決まる。"
msgstr ""
"Bravais lattice types classify arrangements of lattice points, whereas "
"space groups describe the symmetry of the atomic arrangement on the "
"lattice. For example, inversion preserves the atomic arrangement in the "
"\\ :ref:`cubic phase of barium titanate <batio3-crystal-phases>`\\ . \\ "
":ref:`Spontaneous polarization <spontaneous-polarization>`\\  is a polar "
"vector, so it changes sign under inversion. In an inversion-symmetric "
"structure, :math:`\\boldsymbol P` and :math:`-\\boldsymbol P` represent "
"the polarization of the same structure. The polarization of a periodic "
"crystal is defined only modulo the \\ :ref:`polarization quantum <fo-"
"polarization-quantum>`\\ , so this condition becomes :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"P\\equiv-\\boldsymbol P` modulo that quantum. Each component of the "
"polarization is therefore either zero or half the quantum. In either "
"case, an inversion-symmetric structure \\ :ref:`has no spontaneous "
"polarization <polarization-inversion>`, because spontaneous polarization "
"is measured as the change in polarization from an inversion-symmetric "
"reference structure. In the tetragonal phase, inversion symmetry is lost "
"and polarization along the long axis is allowed. Whether polarization "
"actually occurs, and how large it is, depend on the atomic displacements "
"and electronic states."

